  "query_preview": "though with some rain chances, mainly on Friday and late \nSunday into Monday.\n\nAn upper level ridge will anchor itself over the southeast US \nthrough the weekend. Our area will be on the northern periphery of \nthe ridge, with a modest west/northwest flow. This will result in \nseasonable temperatures through the weekend and into next week with \nhighs generally in the 80s. \n\nA few shortwaves will impinge on the ridge, driving multiple rounds \nof low pressure through our area. This will result in a few chances \nfor showers and thunderstorms, first on Friday, mainly for the \nsouthern half of the area. More widespread rain looks to come Sunday \nNight into Monday, which could also include a few thunderstorms. \nHowever, the risk for impactful and significant weather \n(severe/flash flooding) appears low at this time. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...There is the potential for minor tidal flooding \nduring the evening high tides this week along the Atlantic coast, \nDelaware Bay, and tidal Delaware River, especially with this \nevening's high tide.\n\nThe New Moon is today and as a result astronomical tides for this \nevening's high tide cycle will be near or over minor flooding \nthresholds for many places along the Atlantic coasts of New Jersey \nand Delware, Delaware Bay, and the tidal Delaware River. A Coastal \nFlood Advisory for this evening remains in effect for all areas \nalong the Delaware Bay as well as along the Atlantic coast from Cape \nMay County Southward. The highest astronomical tides will occur this \nevening but the threat of minor tidal flooding may linger through \nThursday or Friday as well.\n\nTidal flooding is not currently forecast for the Eastern Shore of \nthe Chesapeake Bay.",
